{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Eaters of bread</b> — in sorrow." "And the sense of <b>those who rise early</b> — to the market." "And likewise <b>those who sit late</b> — there." "<b>So He gives</b> — HaShem mentioned above, to His beloved." "<b>Sleep</b> — in the manner of sweet sleep of the worker. And behold, the whole matter is decreed from heaven, and to all HaShem gives as He decreed — not according to a person's thought, his running, and his toil and stratagems."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 127, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:22.410327935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}